The numbers is a list of 1, 2, 2, 3, and 1.
The counts is a list of 100 zeros.
The firsts is an empty list of whole numbers.
The lasts is an empty list of whole numbers.
For every spot from 0 to 99.
Place -1 into firsts.
Place -1 into lasts.

The last is the last position of numbers.
For every spot from 0 to last.
The value is item spot of numbers.
Set item value of counts to item value of counts plus 1.
If item value of firsts is -1, set item value of firsts to spot.
Set item value of lasts to spot.

The degree is 0.
For every value from 0 to 99.
If item value of counts is more than degree, set degree to item value of counts.

The best is 1000000.
For every value from 0 to 99.
If item value of counts is degree.
The width is item value of lasts minus item value of firsts plus 1.
If width is less than best, set best to width.

Show best.
